  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The M – diagonal pass and finish at speed",
  "description": "Two lines, one in each corner beside the goal, with a high cone on each side further out. The first in one line runs without the ball down and around their cone. The first in the other line plays a diagonal pass to the runner, who shoots first time near the cone. Then the passer runs around their cone and gets the pass from the other side, and so on. The running paths make an M.\n\nSwap lines so everyone shoots from both sides. A quick warm-up for both players and goalkeeper. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pass along the floor, to the blade."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The runner shows with the stick where they want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Shoot first time – do not stop the ball first."
    }
  ],
